("card:PART 4 · THE WEST LANDING", ""),
# ACT 3 — crisis
("muirhead:x", "Three days after the discovery, the lighthouse board sent its superintendent, Robert Muirhead. He knew these men. He had helped choose them."),
("char:think|coat", "First, he looked at the coats. Moore had told him something important. The keepers only wore their sea boots and oilskins when they went down to the landings, by the water."),
("keepers:3", "Ducat was missing his sea boots and his waterproof. Marshall was missing his sea boots and oilskins. So those two had gone down to the sea, on purpose, dressed for bad weather."),
("char:curious|q", "But MacArthur's coat was still on its hook. So why would he leave in such a hurry that he didn't even grab it?"),
("slate:x", "Then there was the slate, where the keepers chalked notes before copying them into the official log. The last notes were from the morning of the fifteenth of December. The same day the light went dark."),
("landing:x", "And then Muirhead went down to the west landing, on the side of the island that faces the open Atlantic. What he saw there changed everything."),
("storm:gale", "There had been a heavy storm in the days before. The keepers knew it. They had noted the weather themselves. And the west landing had taken a beating."),
("landing:x", "Iron railings were bent out of shape. A box that held ropes and equipment, wedged into a crack in the rocks high above the waterline, had vanished. Big pieces of turf had been ripped off the cliff, far above where waves normally reach."),
("char:shock|wave", "The sea had climbed higher than anyone thought possible, and taken heavy things with it. But that's not the strangest part."),
("char:think|q", "The strangest part is that the damage was high. Very high. Which means that if the men were down there at the wrong moment, there would have been nowhere to run."),
