# LESSON
("char:think|q", "So why did a simple, sad accident turn into one of the most famous mysteries in the world?"),
("char:curious|book", "Because our brains hate empty spaces. When we don't know what happened, we fill the gap. And we usually fill it with the scariest thing we can imagine."),
("char:point|fake", "A poem added a fallen chair. A magazine added a crying keeper. And a hundred years later, millions of people believe it, because it's a better story than the truth."),
("char:point|book", "So next time you hear a terrifying story online, ask one simple question. Who wrote that down, and when? You'll be surprised how often the scariest detail is the newest one."),
("char:sad|heart", "The truth is that the most dangerous moments in life often don't look dramatic. They look like a chore. A quick job you've done a hundred times. Just one more trip down to the landing."),
